{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally in China", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Time for Tea", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify  health problems and ways of staying healthy, and use them in a limited range of social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "blanket ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a wool or cotton covering on a bed that helps you keep warm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need a blanket to keep warm.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to write about food or drink.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "harmful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing damage or harm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Pollution is harmful to the environment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pass", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go by", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They won't let a single day pass without a cup of tea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "material", "type": "name"}, {"content": "what something is made of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My pillow is made of soft material.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "authentic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "made in the traditional or original way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love authentic Chinese food!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to claim", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say something is true", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some people claim that tea is good for you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the home of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "where something started", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: China is the home of tea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to convince", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause someone to believe something or change their mind", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You use persuasive language to convince someone.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Persuasive Language", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use persuasive language to convince the reader to agree with you about an issue. You use facts to give your opinion.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Words like <span class=\"strong\">fabulous</span>, <span class=\"strong\">best</span>, <span class=\"strong\">amazing</span> and <span class=\"strong\">special</span> can persuade someone to believe something.</br></br>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">Chinese tea is the best tea in the world!</span></br> </br>Advertisements often use persuasive writing. They use words like <span class=\"strong\">amazing</span>, <span class=\"strong\">brilliant</span> or <span class=\"strong\">free</span> to persuade customers.</br> You can also use persuasive writing to convince someone that you are right and/or that they are wrong.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use persuasive writing, think about your audience. </br><li>Who are you selling to or trying to persuade?</br><li> Choose words that your audience understands. </br><li>List your key points. Think about how to organize your writing. How many paragraphs?</br></br>Language you can use when you are making an argument.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Persuasive Writing Aspects\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Examples\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Showing Contrast (another idea)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Coffee is good. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">However</span>, excess of coffee can hurt you.    Sugar gives you energy. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">On the other hand</span>, it has many calories.     <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Although</span> chocolate is delicious, a large amount can give you a headache and stomach ache. Wine is tasty. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Unfortunately</span>, it has a lot of calories.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ordering\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can eat healthily. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">First of all</span>, eat at regular hours. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Then</span>, try to avoid saturated fat. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Next</span>, control the amount of food you eat. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Finally</span>, never forget to have your daily meals.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Summarizing, Concluding\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">To sum up</span>, drinking tea is a very healthy habit.  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">In summary</span>, breakfast is the most important daily meal.  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">All things considered</span>, don't eat too much meat, principally red meat.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adding more\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tea is a very healthy drink. <span class=\\\"strong\\\">What's more</span>, black tea is the healthiest type.  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">In addition to making you</span> healthy, daily exercise will make you fit. Sleeping well <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will not (won't) only</span> help your body relax, <span class=\\\"strong\\\">but</span> it will <span class=\\\"strong\\\">also</span> make your memory better.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Research food and drink that help with health problems.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Complete the table below.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose three items and write a sentence for each.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your sentences to a partner or family member.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Food or Drink&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What Does It Help?&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>&nbsp;<br/>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research food and drink.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the information with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write three sentences about food and health.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can write a small persuasive text about food and customs.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can ask and report about things and events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about common health problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you drink tea? What kind?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you think tea can help an upset stomach?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_fe